{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "b1f4a9d0-7c3e-4f2a-9a41-ph-healthcare-001",
		"name": "PH Healthcare System — Backend API",
		"description": "Full API collection for the PH Healthcare backend (Express 5 + Prisma + bKash + Redis).\n\n## Setup\n1. Import `PH-Healthcare.postman_environment.json` and select it (baseUrl defaults to `http://localhost:4000`, matching `PORT` in .env).\n2. Start the server (`npm run dev`). It seeds:\n   - SUPER_ADMIN — `superadmin@gmail.com` / `Admin123`\n   - DOCTOR — `doctor@gmail.com` / `Doctor123`\n3. Run **Auth → Login (Super Admin)** and **Auth → Login (Doctor)** — tokens are captured automatically into `adminToken` / `doctorToken`.\n4. For a patient: **Auth → Register Patient** → read the OTP from your email → set the `otp` variable → **Auth → Verify Email** → **Auth → Login (Patient)**.\n\n## Auth mechanism\nThe `auth()` middleware reads the token from the `accessToken` cookie first, then falls back to the `Authorization` header (with or without the `Bearer ` prefix). This collection uses the Authorization header with per-role variables so admin, doctor and patient sessions can be held at the same time.\n\n## Suggested run order\nAuth → Doctor (apply / verify / approve) → Schedule (create / publish) → Appointment (book → pay → callback) → Prescription → Payment → Analytics.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"auth": { "type": "noauth" },
	"variable": [
		{ "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:4000", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "apiUrl", "value": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "adminToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "doctorToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "patientToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "refreshToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "patientEmail", "value": "patient1@gmail.com", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "patientPassword", "value": "Patient123", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "adminEmail", "value": "superadmin@gmail.com", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "adminPassword", "value": "Admin123", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "doctorEmail", "value": "doctor@gmail.com", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "doctorPassword", "value": "Doctor123", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "newDoctorEmail", "value": "newdoctor@gmail.com", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "newDoctorPassword", "value": "Doctor123", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "otp", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "doctorId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "scheduleId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "appointmentId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "paymentId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "prescriptionId", "value": "", "type": "string" }
	],
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "00 · Health",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Root — server alive",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": [""] },
						"description": "GET / — returns the welcome payload. Use this to confirm the server, Postgres and Redis all booted."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"pm.test('success flag', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().success).to.eql(true));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "404 — unknown route",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/does-not-exist", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["does-not-exist"] },
						"description": "Exercises the notFound middleware."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": ["pm.test('404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));"]
							}
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "01 · Auth",
			"description": "`/api/v1/auth`. Registration is OTP-gated: register stashes the user in Redis for 10 minutes and emails an OTP; verify-email creates the real User + Patient rows and returns cookies.",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Register Patient",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Test Patient\",\n  \"email\": \"{{patientEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{patientPassword}}\",\n  \"patient\": {\n    \"contactNumber\": \"01700000000\",\n    \"address\": \"Dhaka, Bangladesh\"\n  }\n}"
						},
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/register", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "register"] },
						"description": "Zod-validated: name (3–255), email, password (6–64), optional `patient.contactNumber` / `patient.address`.\n\nNo user row is created yet — an OTP is emailed via Resend and the payload is cached in Redis for 10 minutes. Follow with **Verify Email**."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
									"console.log('Check the inbox for', pm.collectionVariables.get('patientEmail'), 'then set the otp variable.');"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Verify Email (OTP)",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{patientEmail}}\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/verify-email", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "verify-email"] },
						"description": "Set the `otp` variable to the 6-digit code from the registration email first.\n\nCreates the User + Patient records, sends a welcome email and sets the accessToken/refreshToken cookies. The JSON `data` is `null` — tokens only come back as cookies here, so log in afterwards if you want a bearer token."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": ["pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Login (Patient)",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{patientEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{patientPassword}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
						"description": "Saves the access token into `patientToken` and the refresh token into `refreshToken`."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const body = pm.response.json();",
									"if (body && body.data && body.data.accessToken) {",
									"  pm.collectionVariables.set('patientToken', body.data.accessToken);",
									"  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', body.data.refreshToken);",
									"  console.log('patientToken saved');",
									"}"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Login (Super Admin)",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
						"description": "Seeded SUPER_ADMIN (see `src/app/utils/seed.ts`). Saves `adminToken`."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const body = pm.response.json();",
									"if (body && body.data && body.data.accessToken) {",
									"  pm.collectionVariables.set('adminToken', body.data.accessToken);",
									"  console.log('adminToken saved');",
									"}"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Login (Doctor)",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{doctorEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{doctorPassword}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
						"description": "Seeded DOCTOR (`doctor@gmail.com` / `Doctor123`). Saves `doctorToken`."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const body = pm.response.json();",
									"if (body && body.data && body.data.accessToken) {",
									"  pm.collectionVariables.set('doctorToken', body.data.accessToken);",
									"  console.log('doctorToken saved');",
									"}"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Get Me",
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{patientToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/me", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "me"] },
						"description": "Any authenticated role. Swap the bearer variable to `{{adminToken}}` / `{{doctorToken}}` to test other roles. Returns the user with the `patient` relation, password omitted."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": ["pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Refresh Token",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
							{ "key": "Cookie", "value": "refreshToken={{refreshToken}}", "description": "Fallback — the handler reads req.cookies.refreshToken only." }
						],
						"body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{}" },
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/refresh-token", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "refresh-token"] },
						"description": "Reads the refresh token **from the cookie only** — a body or Authorization token is ignored. Postman's cookie jar keeps it after login, so this usually works with no manual header."
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Google Login",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"idToken\": \"PASTE_GOOGLE_ID_TOKEN\"\n}" },
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/google", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "google"] },
						"description": "Requires a real Google ID token issued for the configured GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID.\n\n⚠️ Backend bug: the controller calls `AuthService.googleLogin({ idToken: req.body })` — it wraps the whole body instead of passing `req.body.idToken`, so verification fails even with a valid token. Fix the controller before this route can pass."
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Forget Password",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{patientEmail}}\"\n}" },
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/forget-password", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "forget-password"] },
						"description": "Emails a 6-digit OTP (Redis TTL 5 min). Only for ACTIVE credential users; Google-only accounts are rejected."
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Reset Password",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{patientEmail}}\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\",\n  \"newPassword\": \"NewPass123\"\n}" },
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/reset-password", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "reset-password"] },
						"description": "Set `otp` to the code from the forget-password email. Sends a confirmation email on success."
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Negative — login with wrong password",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"wrongpassword\"\n}" },
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] }
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": ["pm.test('400 Invalid credentials', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));"]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Negative — protected route without token",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/me", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "me"] },
						"description": "Clear the Postman cookie jar for localhost first, otherwise the accessToken cookie from a previous login authenticates the call."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": ["pm.test('401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"]
							}
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "02 · User",
			"description": "`/api/v1/user`",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Upload Profile Image",
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{patientToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
						"method": "PATCH",
						"header": [],
						"body": {
							"mode": "formdata",
							"formdata": [
								{ "key": "profileImage", "type": "file", "src": [], "description": "Pick a local image file. Multer memory storage → Cloudinary upload." }
							]
						},
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/user/profile-image", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["user", "profile-image"] },
						"description": "Any authenticated role. multipart/form-data with a single field named `profileImage`. Returns 400 if no file is attached.\n\nNote: the success message is hard-coded as \"Password reset successfully\" in the controller — cosmetic bug."
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "03 · Doctor",
			"description": "`/api/v1/doctor`. Doctor onboarding is a 3-step flow: apply (OTP email) → verify (multipart, uploads resume) → approve (admin).",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Apply as Doctor",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Dr. New Doctor\",\n  \"email\": \"{{newDoctorEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{newDoctorPassword}}\"\n}" },
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/doctor/apply", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["doctor", "apply"] },
						"description": "Public route. Emails an OTP; continue with **Verify Doctor**."
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Verify Doctor (multipart)",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [],
						"body": {
							"mode": "formdata",
							"formdata": [
								{
									"key": "body",
									"value": "{\"email\":\"{{newDoctorEmail}}\",\"otp\":\"{{otp}}\",\"specialization\":\"Cardiology\",\"licenseNumber\":\"DOC-99887\",\"qualification\":\"MBBS, FCPS\",\"expYear\":8,\"bio\":\"Cardiologist with 8 years of experience.\",\"consultationFee\":\"1500\",\"contactNumber\":\"01711111111\"}",
									"type": "text",
									"description": "The controller reads req.body.body and JSON.parses it — the whole payload must be a JSON STRING in a form field literally named 'body'."
								},
								{ "key": "resume", "type": "file", "src": [], "description": "Required — a single PDF/doc." },
								{ "key": "additionalFiles", "type": "file", "src": [], "description": "Optional, up to 5 files. Duplicate this row for multiple files." }
							]
						},
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/doctor/verify", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["doctor", "verify"] },
						"description": "Public multipart route. Fields: `body` (JSON string), `resume` (1 file), `additionalFiles` (≤5 files).\n\nJSON keys: email, otp, specialization, licenseNumber, qualification, expYear (number), bio?, consultationFee?, contactNumber."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const body = pm.response.json();",
									"const d = body && body.data;",
									"const id = (d && d.id) || (d && d.doctor && d.doctor.id);",
									"if (id) { pm.collectionVariables.set('doctorId', id); console.log('doctorId saved', id); }"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Approve / Reject Doctor",
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{adminToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"doctorId\": \"{{doctorId}}\",\n  \"verificationStatus\": \"APPROVE\",\n  \"rejectionReason\": \"\"\n}" },
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/doctor/approve", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["doctor", "approve"] },
						"description": "ADMIN / SUPER_ADMIN only.\n\n`verificationStatus`: `PENDING` | `APPROVE` | `REJECTED`. Send `rejectionReason` when rejecting."
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Get All Doctors",
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{adminToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{apiUrl}}/doctor/all-doctors?page=1&limit=10&sortBy=createdAt&sortOrder=asc&searchTerm=",
							"host": ["{{apiUrl}}"],
							"path": ["doctor", "all-doctors"],
							"query": [
								{ "key": "page", "value": "1" },
								{ "key": "limit", "value": "10" },
								{ "key": "sortBy", "value": "createdAt", "description": "Any Doctor column: createdAt, name, expYear, consultationFee…" },
								{ "key": "sortOrder", "value": "asc", "description": "asc | desc" },
								{ "key": "searchTerm", "value": "", "description": "Case-insensitive across name, qualification, specialization, licenseNumber." }
							]
						},
						"description": "ADMIN / SUPER_ADMIN only. Paginated and searchable. Captures the first doctor id into `doctorId` if it is still empty."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const d = pm.response.json().data || {};",
									"const list = d.data || d.doctors || (Array.isArray(d) ? d : []);",
									"if (Array.isArray(list) && list.length && !pm.collectionVariables.get('doctorId')) {",
									"  pm.collectionVariables.set('doctorId', list[0].id);",
									"  console.log('doctorId saved', list[0].id);",
									"}"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "04 · Schedule",
			"description": "`/api/v1/schedule`. Doctors create DRAFT schedules; admins publish, update and soft-delete them.",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Create Schedule (Doctor)",
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{doctorToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"startDateTime\": \"2026-09-10T10:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"endDateTime\": \"2026-09-10T13:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"meetingLink\": \"https://meet.google.com/abc-defg-hij\"\n}" },
						"url": { "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/schedule/create-schedule", "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"], "path": ["schedule", "create-schedule"] },
						"description": "DOCTOR only. ISO-8601 datetimes. Saves the created id into `scheduleId`."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
									"const d = pm.response.json().data;",
									"const id = (d && d.id) || (Array.isArray(d) && d[0] && d[0].id);",
									"if (id) { pm.collectionVariables.set('scheduleId', id); console.log('scheduleId saved', id); }"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "My Schedules (Doctor)",
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{doctorToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{apiUrl}}/schedule/my-schedules?page=1&limit=10&status=",
							"host": ["{{apiUrl}}"],
							"path": ["schedule", "my-schedules"],
							"query": [
								{ "key": "page", "value": "1" },
								{ "key": "limit", "value": "10" },
								{ "key": "status", "value": "", "description": "DRAFT | PUBLISHED" }
							]
						},
						"description": "DOCTOR only.\n\n⚠️ Backend bug: the controller passes `req.body` (not `req.query`) into the service, so these query filters are ignored — defaults (page 1, limit 10) always apply."
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "All Schedules (Admin)",
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{adminToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
